    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1015">

                <pb facs="1274" n="1264" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1264"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.42700 SE/3–2647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-07T19:00:00-05:00">April 7, 1947—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>410. On Apr 7 [<hi rendition="#italic">5</hi>] Dept dispatched note to Chinese
                    Ambassador stating readiness open negotiations Washington for agreement to
                    implement Fulbright<anchor n="5" xml:id="d1015-f1"/> program and enclosing draft
                    agreement for study prior negotiation. Depins 293 Mar 26 transmitted draft
                        agreement.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d1015-f2"/> Dept would welcome Embs comments
                    before opening discussions with Chinese here. Cabling program plans
                        soonest.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d1015-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 410, repeated Shanghai 573.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1015-f1" n="5" xml:id="d1015-f1-content">
                <p>Senator J. William Fulbright of Arkansas, author of educational exchange program
                    legislation in Congress.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1015-f2" n="6" xml:id="d1015-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1015-f3" n="7" xml:id="d1015-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
